// Export selector for the cassette, isolated receiver reviews, or the complete
// water system. Normal output is the cassette. Selector 2 was the former
// printable drain plug and is deliberately retired: use the specified
// commercial silicone snap-lock plug.
// 0 = cassette, 1 = receiver, 2 = retired, 3 = receiver cutaway,
// 4 = complete integrated water-system review,
// 5 = standalone tester in functional orientation,
// 6 = standalone tester in upside-down print orientation,
// 8 = all backing-board side hooks, 9 = one side-hook close review,
// 10 = both top hanging snap lips, 11 = front scaffold contacts,
// 12 = one top hanging snap lip close review,
// 13 = center acrylic/image pocket with removable support posts,
// 14 = same pocket after the posts are removed,
// 15 = isolated pocket plus its removable support posts,
// 16 = simple wetting station close review (functional orientation),
// 17 = same close review in upside-down print orientation,
// 18 = unobstructed C-channel/hoop/basin, 19 = same geometry inverted,
// 20 = half-section through the simple wetting station,
// 21 = close review of the wall-rooted two-sided hitch,
// 22 = focused rear-perimeter review of the plain structural center strip,
// 23 = cutaway through the side-fill bore, roof vent, and internal shield,
// 24 = removable roof alone in the established inverted orientation,
// 25 = experimental cassette and roof side-by-side (default review),
// 26 = roof assembled on cassette in functional orientation,
// 27 = roof raised above cassette in functional orientation,
// 28 = colored assembled roof, 29 = colored exploded roof,
// 30 = close section at the -Y wall stop,
// 31 = exploded front retainer pair, 32 = exploded rear retainer pair,
// 33 = one actual retainer beside its actual mating roof fragment
// 34 = experimental two-inch cassette-top and full removable-roof fit coupon,
// 35 = close review of the actual printed horizontal-PVA/wick hardware only,
// 36 = isolated raised PVA redirect profile review,
// 37 = close review of the active 80 mm side-diffuser branch,
// 38 = complete cassette in explicit upside-down print orientation,
// 39 = isolated 80 mm diffuser U/V hitch,
// 40 = isolated pitched drip basket,
// 41 = wet mirrored hitch above the unchanged dry guide,
// 42 = isolated permanent rear-receiver print arch.
// Default to the complete cassette in functional orientation.
